WEBVTT

00:01.360 --> 00:05.400
<i>Ah, it's good to finally be
 back at Saint Noel Academy!</i>

00:05.980 --> 00:12.050
<i>I'd never dreamed a day would come when 
I'd feel happy to come back to this academy.</i>

00:12.050 --> 00:14.320
Princess Mia, it's so good to see you!

00:14.320 --> 00:17.320
Chloe! I hope you've been well?

00:17.320 --> 00:21.230
Yes! And my father sends his regards.

00:21.230 --> 00:26.170
After his meeting with you, he went on and on 
about how you truly are the Wisdom of the empire.

00:26.480 --> 00:30.400
My goodness. I'm afraid he's 
giving me too much credit.

00:30.400 --> 00:32.000
<i>Too much credit indeed.</i>

00:32.000 --> 00:34.970
Mia, Chloe, how lovely to see you.

00:35.390 --> 00:36.680
Princess Rafina!

00:37.240 --> 00:38.590
So lovely to see you.

00:38.590 --> 00:40.500
L-Lovely to see you.

00:41.280 --> 00:45.090
I was not aware the two of you were friends.

00:45.090 --> 00:49.070
Chloe and I often discuss books 
we've read with each other.

00:49.070 --> 00:49.920
Don't we?

00:49.920 --> 00:51.610
Huh? Uh, yes!

00:52.040 --> 00:55.820
Wonderful. I was just about to have tea.

00:55.820 --> 00:57.320
Would you care to join me?

00:57.540 --> 00:59.030
That would be lovely!

00:59.030 --> 01:01.910
Y-You're saying I can join you as well?

01:02.160 --> 01:05.000
Of course. Right, Mia?

01:05.200 --> 01:09.210
Of course. Chloe and I are <i>good friends</i>.

01:09.720 --> 01:11.110
<i>"Good friends"!</i>

01:11.110 --> 01:13.100
Now, let's be on our way.

01:16.000 --> 01:19.180
This reminds me, I heard 
something interesting, Mia.

01:19.730 --> 01:22.130
I heard you're creating a school.

01:22.130 --> 01:23.890
Is that true?

01:24.730 --> 01:29.440
To open the school's doors to 
commoners as well—a bold decision.

01:29.710 --> 01:32.900
Oh?! Yes, that is the plan.

01:33.530 --> 01:36.150
<i>I only chose to make commoners able to attend</i>

01:36.150 --> 01:40.120
<i>because I didn't want to put Tiona's 
brother in a school with only aristocrats.</i>

01:40.510 --> 01:45.080
I-Is that really so shocking? 
It doesn't strike me as all that strange.

01:45.080 --> 01:48.790
Talent has nothing to do 
with lineage, after all...

01:49.300 --> 01:50.130
Right?

01:53.040 --> 01:55.600
Truly, it's exactly as you say!

01:55.600 --> 01:59.220
This is why I feel lucky and proud 
to count you as a friend, Mia!

01:59.830 --> 02:05.060
<i>The excuse Mia came up with in 
desperation pierced Rafina's heart!</i>

02:06.410 --> 02:09.270
Wh-Why, you flatter me, Princess Rafina!

02:09.270 --> 02:11.970
<i>And so Mia ran with it!</i>

02:11.970 --> 02:14.190
<i>I've avoided my fate at the guillotine,</i>

02:14.190 --> 02:16.700
<i>and now the tide has turned 
thoroughly in my favor.</i>

02:16.700 --> 02:21.120
<i>Truly, a huge wave has come my way!</i>

02:22.330 --> 02:23.830
Pardon my intrusion!

02:24.510 --> 02:26.640
P-Princess Mia.

02:26.640 --> 02:28.040
Anne?

02:28.510 --> 02:31.630
Is something the matter? You seem frantic.

02:32.890 --> 02:34.090
There's been...

02:35.050 --> 02:36.920
There's been a revolution!

02:38.400 --> 02:39.300
What?

02:40.010 --> 02:42.970
A-A revolution?

02:46.720 --> 02:49.730
H-How could that be?

02:50.190 --> 02:53.690
<i>I went to such great effort. 
What was it all for?</i>

02:53.950 --> 02:58.940
S-Stay calm! The revolution didn't 
occur in the Tearmoon Empire!

02:59.600 --> 03:00.220
What?

03:01.000 --> 03:05.170
It happened in the Kingdom of Remno!

03:07.070 --> 03:09.340
<i>The Kingdom of... Remno?</i>

04:40.340 --> 04:45.510
<b>Episode 9: Princess Mia's (Love-Focused) Choice</b>

04:40.870 --> 04:44.690
A revolution? In Remno?

04:44.690 --> 04:47.390
Excuse our intrusion, Princess Rafina.

04:47.730 --> 04:50.720
We heard that Princess Mia was here.

04:51.190 --> 04:52.840
Prince Sion...

04:55.210 --> 04:57.600
All of you, please, take a seat.

04:57.960 --> 04:59.600
I'll prepare some tea.

05:01.470 --> 05:04.950
Now, please, continue.

05:05.340 --> 05:08.260
You say there was a revolution in Remno?

05:08.260 --> 05:13.350
More precisely, it's progressed to a 
popular uprising and calls for revolution.

05:13.350 --> 05:17.670
So then there still hasn't 
been a revolution yet, right?

05:17.990 --> 05:23.190
According to Sunkland's intelligence 
agency, the Wind Ravens...

05:25.070 --> 05:30.150
"Signs of an insurrection that may lead 
to overthrow of the throne in Remno."

05:30.150 --> 05:33.830
"Military intervention by 
Sunkland will be needed"

05:33.830 --> 05:38.310
"to protect the populace 
from expected oppression."

05:38.570 --> 05:43.360
After receiving this report, 
I felt I ought to inform Princess Mia.

05:43.360 --> 05:47.010
The only information we have is that 
there are signs of an insurrection,

05:47.480 --> 05:50.950
but it's a fact that the political 
situation there is precarious.

05:50.950 --> 05:53.510
The situation is precarious?

05:53.510 --> 05:55.040
Could you elaborate?

05:55.440 --> 05:59.220
The Kingdom of Remno already has 
heavy taxes placed on its subjects

05:59.220 --> 06:01.420
to maintain its powerful military.

06:01.940 --> 06:05.170
But they've supposedly proposed 
a further tax increase.

06:05.620 --> 06:08.380
There would naturally be 
some voices in opposition.

06:10.160 --> 06:12.970
So, as to represent the 
discontent of the populace,

06:12.970 --> 06:18.310
Chancellor of the Kingdom of Remno 
Count Dasayev Donovan spoke against it first.

06:18.690 --> 06:22.230
I am also familiar with Chancellor Dasayev.

06:22.230 --> 06:24.900
I understood him to be a 
wise and temperate man.

06:25.200 --> 06:30.830
Yes. It appears he was in fact acting to mediate
 between the populace and the royal family.

06:30.830 --> 06:31.980
But...

06:31.980 --> 06:36.250
But something happened in the 
Kingdom of Remno. That's the takeaway.

06:36.710 --> 06:37.560
I suspect so.

06:38.350 --> 06:40.460
<i>What's going on?</i>

06:40.460 --> 06:45.420
<i>Just when I'd escaped the guillotine 
and everything had worked out...</i>

06:42.690 --> 06:45.420
I'm comin' for ya!

06:46.220 --> 06:51.210
<i>I don't have any memory of a revolution 
happening in Remno in the prior timeline.</i>

06:51.210 --> 06:54.960
<i>And if there had been a revolution 
or uprising in some other country,</i>

06:54.960 --> 06:56.890
<i>I would remember it.</i>

06:56.890 --> 06:59.090
<i>Of all the places it could've been,</i>

06:59.090 --> 07:01.400
<i>why did it have to be the Kingdom of Remno?</i>

07:01.960 --> 07:07.110
<i>W-Well, regardless, the best thing 
is to stay away from any jeopardy.</i>

07:11.430 --> 07:12.810
Prince Abel...

07:14.180 --> 07:16.290
Princess Mia, do you want to go there?

07:16.780 --> 07:17.740
Huh?

07:17.740 --> 07:21.250
You look like you're on the verge of tears.

07:24.480 --> 07:25.900
Don't be silly.

07:27.120 --> 07:31.900
<i>All this time, I've been doing everything 
I can to avoid the guillotine.</i>

07:33.190 --> 07:36.560
<i>To now choose to enter a maelstrom 
of an impending revolution...</i>

07:36.560 --> 07:38.150
<i>That would be...</i>

07:43.880 --> 07:45.020
<i>And yet...</i>

07:46.710 --> 07:48.230
I do wish to go...

07:48.510 --> 07:51.740
I want to see Prince Abel!

07:56.020 --> 07:59.310
Please, would you aid me in my desire?

08:00.470 --> 08:04.600
I'm afraid that is easier said than done.

08:04.600 --> 08:07.960
Yes. We'll need to come up 
with some sort of plan.

08:08.300 --> 08:11.810
Do you mean to say our only 
option is to operate in secret?

08:11.810 --> 08:13.810
There must be a way.

08:13.810 --> 08:15.730
Let's stay calm and figure this out.

08:16.160 --> 08:17.680
Right, Mia?

08:18.730 --> 08:19.820
Thank you...

08:20.360 --> 08:21.900
U-Um...

08:22.620 --> 08:27.160
My parents' trading group is 
sending a caravan to Remno soon.

08:27.160 --> 08:30.320
What if you used that as a cover?

08:30.770 --> 08:32.280
Chloe...

08:32.680 --> 08:35.360
Princess Mia, I'm sure this will work out.

08:35.790 --> 08:40.800
Merchants would certainly be unlikely 
to draw the ire of the populace.

08:40.800 --> 08:41.950
Then it's settled.

08:42.610 --> 08:43.960
In that case, I'll go as well.

08:44.810 --> 08:47.610
Your Highness, I appreciate your intentions.

08:47.610 --> 08:50.070
But consider your position!

08:50.070 --> 08:52.440
I <i>have</i> considered it.

08:52.440 --> 08:55.540
The princess of a major power is 
planning to head into a dangerous area

08:55.540 --> 08:58.050
out of concern for a schoolmate's safety.

08:58.050 --> 09:00.240
Prince Sion...

09:00.240 --> 09:02.770
Princess Mia, I shall accompany you as well.

09:03.610 --> 09:06.850
I have a some skill with a sword.

09:06.850 --> 09:08.730
I'll do whatever I can to protect you!

09:09.390 --> 09:10.770
Tiona...

09:12.300 --> 09:17.660
I can explain how the caravan 
works, so come to my room.

09:21.620 --> 09:22.510
Anne.

09:22.510 --> 09:23.330
Yes?

09:23.830 --> 09:28.540
Since you can't ride a horse, 
I'm afraid I can't take you along.

09:28.540 --> 09:31.630
What?! But Princess Mia...

09:31.960 --> 09:35.740
Don't worry. I promise I'll come back.

09:35.740 --> 09:38.030
So what I need from you

09:38.030 --> 09:40.300
is for you to stay and focus on your job.

09:41.470 --> 09:42.750
Do you understand?

09:50.420 --> 09:52.190
Princess Mia...

09:52.190 --> 09:55.070
Hold your head up, Anne.

09:55.450 --> 09:59.790
You don't have time to be down 
on yourself. Isn't that so?

10:00.300 --> 10:03.950
But I... I'm ashamed of myself.

10:04.420 --> 10:09.000
Princess Mia showed such 
concern for my safety,

10:09.000 --> 10:12.970
and yet I can't help her. 
I'll only be a burden.

10:14.320 --> 10:16.190
Anne, do you remember?

10:16.740 --> 10:20.140
Mia called you her confidante.

10:21.430 --> 10:24.320
Anne is my confidante.

10:25.200 --> 10:26.840
Her confidante...

10:26.840 --> 10:30.600
Mia told you to focus on your job.

10:31.310 --> 10:35.610
As her confidante, aren't there 
tasks that only you can perform?

10:36.190 --> 10:38.530
Things only I can do?

10:41.030 --> 10:42.830
E-Excuse me!

10:54.070 --> 10:56.110
It's been three days since 
we left the academy.

10:56.110 --> 11:00.840
Princess Mia must be 
worried sick about Prince Abel.

11:01.200 --> 11:04.710
The place we're headed is 
dangerous enough as it is.

11:04.710 --> 11:08.810
I'm sure even someone like 
Princess Mia can't help but be nervous.

11:09.420 --> 11:11.490
<i>I feel sick!</i>

11:11.490 --> 11:16.020
<i>I didn't think a merchant's 
carriage would shake this much...</i>

11:17.560 --> 11:19.030
We'll be crossing the border soon.

11:19.670 --> 11:22.070
It looks like this is going to work out.

11:22.070 --> 11:26.310
Between Chloe's plan and our 
intelligence agency's route,

11:26.310 --> 11:28.210
it would appear the pieces 
have come together.

11:30.430 --> 11:31.460
What's that?

11:33.670 --> 11:34.960
A bandit!

11:34.960 --> 11:37.050
It's a bandit attack!

11:37.050 --> 11:38.040
A bandit?!

11:38.040 --> 11:39.590
Princess Mia, this way.

11:39.590 --> 11:41.130
Wh-What are you do—

11:43.300 --> 11:44.890
That's a bandit?

11:44.890 --> 11:47.470
Goodness. To frighten a lady...

11:48.170 --> 11:49.930
I can't say I approve!

11:51.980 --> 11:55.610
Well, it would appear you're 
no run-of-the-mill bandit.

11:57.540 --> 11:59.530
His movements aren't amateur...

11:59.870 --> 12:01.790
Who are you?

12:02.490 --> 12:04.700
Your Highness, be careful.

12:04.700 --> 12:07.500
He seems to have a target in mind.

12:09.750 --> 12:11.750
Great. More of you, eh?

12:12.250 --> 12:14.460
Th-They're attacking!

12:16.970 --> 12:19.600
To intentionally delay the
 timing of their attacks...

12:19.600 --> 12:21.630
That's some trouble they're going to.

12:23.640 --> 12:25.840
What do we do, Prince Shion?

12:26.170 --> 12:29.290
It seems like they're drawing in closer!

12:29.290 --> 12:30.680
Stay close to me.

12:32.390 --> 12:35.020
I'm not sure how much I can control that...

12:39.320 --> 12:40.280
Princess Mia!

12:43.780 --> 12:45.320
Princess Mia!

12:50.520 --> 12:52.880
Princess Mia! Answer me!

12:52.880 --> 12:53.870
Princess Mia!

12:56.310 --> 12:58.590
Prince Sion?

12:59.240 --> 13:01.060
<i>Oh, that's right.</i>

13:01.060 --> 13:04.050
<i>I fell from the carriage into the river...</i>

13:04.050 --> 13:05.130
Princess Mia!

13:06.050 --> 13:10.960
<i>I feel like I've read about a situation 
like this in Elise's stories...</i>

13:10.960 --> 13:15.770
<i>In order to restart the drowned 
person's breathing, the prince...</i>

13:16.150 --> 13:17.480
<i>He...</i>

13:17.950 --> 13:20.690
<i>I'm not going to get kissed, am I?</i>

13:20.690 --> 13:21.820
<i>No!</i>

13:21.820 --> 13:26.150
<i>I wanted Prince Abel to be my first kiss.</i>

13:26.840 --> 13:28.580
<i>But still...</i>

13:32.100 --> 13:35.330
<i>Sunkland artificial respiration technique:</i>

13:35.330 --> 13:39.540
<i>If you pull a person from the water, 
immediately turn their head to the side...</i>

13:40.020 --> 13:41.130
Huh?

13:43.240 --> 13:48.180
<i>and use fingers or other implements to 
remove foreign material from their mouth.</i>

13:48.460 --> 13:54.640
<i>Thanks to Sion taking appropriate action, 
Mia's first kiss remained untaken.</i>

13:55.010 --> 13:57.020
I'm so glad you've come to.

13:57.790 --> 14:00.060
I thought I was going to die.

14:00.500 --> 14:03.200
It was certainly a dangerous current.

14:03.200 --> 14:04.690
<i>Not that part!</i>

14:06.690 --> 14:10.160
Th-Thank you for saving me.

14:10.650 --> 14:12.780
It may be a little early to thank me.

14:13.080 --> 14:13.870
Huh?

14:14.580 --> 14:16.490
Where are we?

14:16.490 --> 14:18.910
Downstream from where 
you fell into the river.

14:18.910 --> 14:22.790
We're most likely in northwestern Remno...

14:23.130 --> 14:27.600
So that means we managed to enter 
the Kingdom of Remno, right?

14:27.600 --> 14:29.280
True, we did enter.

14:29.280 --> 14:32.060
But we're likely a great 
distance from the capital,

14:32.060 --> 14:34.140
and we'll have to cross those mountains.

14:34.950 --> 14:36.240
Cross those?

14:43.360 --> 14:46.990
At least now we won't catch a cold.

14:47.400 --> 14:50.700
It's so helpful that you 
knew how to start a fire.

14:51.020 --> 14:54.410
Well, I learned how on hunting trips...

14:59.430 --> 15:01.080
<i>Oh...</i>

15:01.080 --> 15:03.500
<i>So even the perfect superman Prince Sion</i>

15:03.500 --> 15:07.800
<i>has this adorable reaction to 
seeing a girl in undergarments.</i>

15:08.180 --> 15:12.240
<i>I mean, I can't say I'm not 
at least a little embarrassed,</i>

15:12.240 --> 15:15.010
<i>but still, I am a grown woman.</i>

15:15.010 --> 15:19.380
<i>I'm calm enough to watch a pretty boy blush.</i>

15:19.380 --> 15:22.230
<i>A no-good grown woman.</i>

15:22.690 --> 15:27.940
It was also helpful but surprising 
that you could identify edible plants.

15:27.940 --> 15:30.360
It was nothing special.

15:30.360 --> 15:37.080
<i>After all, I once spent a night in the wild 
being chased by the revolutionary army!</i>

15:37.080 --> 15:40.030
<i>That was a tough experience...</i>

15:41.670 --> 15:45.520
<i>But now I'm a survival specialist!</i>

15:45.520 --> 15:49.560
<i>I've researched all the food 
available on the continent.</i>

15:49.560 --> 15:52.550
<i>A fierce tenacity for staying alive.</i>

15:54.460 --> 15:56.250
By the way, Prince Sion...

15:56.250 --> 15:58.630
There's something I'd like to ask you.

15:58.630 --> 16:00.480
Oh? What is it?

16:00.480 --> 16:05.160
If you should learn Prince Abel contributed 
to the oppression of his people,

16:05.160 --> 16:07.040
what will you do?

16:07.740 --> 16:10.070
That's a very sudden question.

16:10.670 --> 16:16.120
Will you condemn even your schoolmate 
if you think his hands aren't clean?

16:19.230 --> 16:22.510
If Prince Abel raised his 
sword against the populace,

16:22.510 --> 16:25.830
I would probably have 
to turn my sword on him.

16:26.150 --> 16:29.850
Depending on the situation, 
you might kill him?

16:30.610 --> 16:33.050
That's your thinking on the matter?

16:34.000 --> 16:37.010
But what other choice would I have?

16:37.610 --> 16:39.810
There's nothing I could do about it.

16:40.760 --> 16:42.440
Is that truly so?

16:42.440 --> 16:43.350
What?

16:44.010 --> 16:45.950
There was no other choice.

16:45.950 --> 16:50.150
Don't you only get to say that if you 
tried everything you possibly could?

16:50.520 --> 16:52.750
"Everything you possibly could"...

16:54.110 --> 16:57.500
<i>It's only natural to condemn 
those who have done evil.</i>

16:57.500 --> 17:02.900
<i>But this wasn't the first time
I've heard of unrest in Remno.</i>

17:02.900 --> 17:05.210
<i>And yet, I never tried 
to do anything about it.</i>

17:05.540 --> 17:09.520
<i>Given that, do I have the 
right to condemn Prince Abel?</i>

17:09.520 --> 17:12.010
<i>Is that what Princess Mia is getting at?</i>

17:12.920 --> 17:16.680
<i>Don't tell me this idiot was thinking 
there was no other choice</i>

17:16.680 --> 17:19.580
<i>when he sent me to the guillotine, too.</i>

17:19.580 --> 17:23.140
<i>Mia was furious for a 
completely different reason.</i>

17:23.490 --> 17:27.350
<i>I mean, I wasn't anywhere 
close to perfect then either.</i>

17:27.350 --> 17:32.830
<i>But couldn't he have done me the favor 
of saying, "Your behavior is a problem,"</i>

17:32.830 --> 17:35.820
<i>before things got to a revolution?</i>

17:38.490 --> 17:41.850
<i>Things might have gone differently if he had,</i>

17:41.850 --> 17:45.120
<i>given my sagacious judgment...</i>

17:45.420 --> 17:48.600
<i>The latter half is not 
without room for doubt.</i>

17:48.600 --> 17:52.670
<i>To just show up when it's too late 
and say there's no other choice,</i>

17:52.670 --> 17:55.340
<i>that's just too cruel!</i>

17:55.690 --> 18:00.930
<i>Or could Princess Mia be proposing 
we stop the revolution itself?</i>

18:01.330 --> 18:04.020
<i>Before Prince Abel does any evil...</i>

18:05.250 --> 18:10.750
<i>Prince Sion's wild imaginings would 
grow steadily wilder from there.</i>

18:13.600 --> 18:15.610
Are you all right, Princess Mia?

18:15.880 --> 18:18.570
I-I'm not all right at all.

18:19.050 --> 18:24.040
This is all the fault of those 
bandits who attacked the carriage.

18:24.580 --> 18:26.840
Bandits, huh...

18:26.840 --> 18:28.750
Is something wrong?

18:29.020 --> 18:33.960
No. I was just wondering if it was 
really bandits we encountered.

18:33.960 --> 18:35.670
What do you mean?

18:36.270 --> 18:39.970
They were clearly combat-trained assassins.

18:39.970 --> 18:43.970
There's a high probability they 
were after either me or you.

18:44.340 --> 18:49.770
But no one should have known 
we were riding in that carriage.

18:49.770 --> 18:53.400
The normal conclusion would be that 
the information leaked somehow.

18:53.710 --> 18:55.000
But that's...

18:55.490 --> 18:58.610
Whatever the case, we need 
to reach the capital quickly.

18:58.860 --> 19:05.080
Saying that doesn't change that we've 
been walking forever, and I'm hungry.

19:05.990 --> 19:10.270
Oh, what a pretty mushroom!

19:10.790 --> 19:13.330
Wait, this reminds me of something...

19:13.790 --> 19:18.950
It's exceedingly difficult to distinguish 
the poison mushrooms from the safe ones.

19:18.950 --> 19:20.970
If you're not an expert,
 it's best to leave them be.

19:21.350 --> 19:24.260
<i>That's what the head chef said.</i>

19:24.660 --> 19:28.560
But if it's this pretty, 
then it's definitely safe to eat!

19:28.560 --> 19:30.980
I wouldn't if I were you!

19:34.600 --> 19:35.440
Who are you?

19:35.440 --> 19:39.600
Lassy, those mushrooms are called Salamandrakes.

19:39.600 --> 19:42.930
They're so toxic, you'll get a 
rash just from touching them.

19:42.930 --> 19:45.180
Oh, they are?

19:45.180 --> 19:48.700
More importantly, you kids 
ain't from around here, are ya?

19:48.700 --> 19:50.040
Where'd you come from?

19:50.380 --> 19:52.080
We—

19:53.190 --> 19:56.050
We should hide our identities.

19:56.050 --> 19:56.960
Got it?

19:59.100 --> 20:01.300
Why don't we start with who you are?

20:01.730 --> 20:02.860
Me?

20:02.860 --> 20:07.010
I'm a hunter from nearby 
Doni Village. Name's Mujik.

20:07.450 --> 20:08.930
A hunter...

20:08.930 --> 20:12.110
We're both the children of merchants.

20:12.110 --> 20:15.310
Bandits attacked, and we were 
separated from our parents.

20:15.310 --> 20:18.480
Whoa, that sounds rough!

20:18.480 --> 20:22.480
Our village is close by. 
You're welcome to come with me.

20:22.480 --> 20:24.430
My! How kind!

20:24.430 --> 20:25.660
Wait, Mia.

20:27.070 --> 20:28.830
We're grateful for the offer,

20:28.830 --> 20:32.660
but we need to reach the 
capital as soon as possible.

20:32.660 --> 20:37.040
The capital, ya say? 
But it'll be sundown soon.

20:37.410 --> 20:41.130
I can see if anyone from the 
village is headed there tomorrow.

20:41.670 --> 20:44.840
You heard him. Let's go.

20:47.550 --> 20:49.760
Welp, this is my place.

20:50.560 --> 20:51.470
Oh, my!

20:51.960 --> 20:54.020
What's this dish?

20:54.020 --> 20:57.830
My special rabbit stew. It's tasty!

20:57.830 --> 21:00.190
That sounds lovely.

21:01.810 --> 21:04.020
This is quite delicious!

21:04.020 --> 21:05.760
I'm glad you like it.

21:05.760 --> 21:07.910
There's plenty more, 
so eat as much as you like.

21:08.200 --> 21:09.330
I will!

21:10.510 --> 21:12.040
Somethin' wrong?

21:12.040 --> 21:13.370
Oh, uh, no.

21:13.880 --> 21:17.940
By the way, there's an insurrection 
going on in Remno, right?

21:17.940 --> 21:20.170
Yup. I'm impressed you know that.

21:20.490 --> 21:22.880
That hasn't caused any 
disturbances in this area?

21:23.340 --> 21:24.530
Nope.

21:24.530 --> 21:26.770
Ain't nobody but country folk here.

21:26.770 --> 21:28.780
We've got our hands full 
with our normal work.

21:28.780 --> 21:31.310
Nobody has time for that stuff.

21:31.710 --> 21:36.020
<i>I remember famine doesn't strike the 
continent for several more years.</i>

21:36.020 --> 21:43.230
<i>It seems odd that a revolution is about 
to occur when food is normally available.</i>

21:44.180 --> 21:49.450
<i>It's so hard to think about 
weighty subjects without sweets.</i>

21:50.210 --> 21:53.540
<i>Mia immediately stopped thinking about it.</i>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
Illustration by: Nami Hidaka
